A1. A little round thing attached to a bottle. ~ BABY
A5. This is handed to a convict to strengthen his conviction. ~ TRACT
A10. Ex-steppe son. ~ TSAR
A14. This kind of body is all at sea. ~ ABLE
A15. A Christmas house-dress. ~ HOLLY
A16. This Spanish duke got in Dutch with the Dutch. ~ ALVA
A17. These are devoted to raising fish. ~ REELS
A19. A member of the F. F. A.s (First Family of Africa). ~ APE
A20. It's dangerous to talk freely in this state. ~ SLEEP
A21. The kind of bodies astronomers see thru their telescopes. ~ STELLAR
A23. Mickey, Jimmy and Johnny. ~ WALKERS
A25. What Omar went thru to get out of an argument. ~ DOOR
A26. Extract of a cow of French extraction. ~ LAIT
A27. Jr's. advance agent (abbr.). ~ SR
A29. Irrigators of the Great American Desert. ~ WETS
A31. A descending seale. ~ WAGE
A32. Tom Heflin's first speech, before he swallowed his rattle. ~ DA
A34. Bean pots. ~ HATS
A36. Skylights. ~ STARS
A38. Modern equivalent of shirt, corset, pantalets, three petticoats and a bustle. ~ SLIP
A40. A seer. ~ EYE
A41. This detective jugged 'em before he caught 'em. ~ ALI
A42. Girl's name, rather close to the clinging variety. ~ IVA
A43. A jungle blade. ~ BOLO
A45. Headlock. ~ TRESS
A47. What Willie could do after they washed his ears. ~ HEAR
